            <ArticleTitle>Silicon diimide gel as an efficient stationary phase in thin layer chromatography for acid-sensitive organic compounds.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>11080-11082</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7cc04952h</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the use of mesoporous silicon diimide gel as a basic stationary phase in thin layer chromatography for the characterisation and purification of acid-sensitive compounds. The gel is prepared by a simple sol-gel process and exhibits a large specific surface area, almost monodisperse pores and basic properties due to free-hanging amine groups.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
